+# Unified source and self-hosted database
+
+Canonical repository: javanwebi/atlasforza. Frontend: src/. Express backend: server.ts, api/, server/db/. Both ship in the root Dockerfile. This import includes the previous auth validation and left-image/right-form fixes from source commit 4a915c547d4ce9fb60928adbe25e4601e0a17c40. Server-only Nginx and Docker configuration changes are not a substitute for an audited server export.
+
+## Database
+
+Set DATA_BACKEND=postgres and DATABASE_SCHEMA=adopted. DATABASE_URL must identify the owner's self-hosted PostgreSQL; SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY must identify Auth from the SAME installation. Keep credentials outside Git. A remote preview cannot use localhost to reach the owner's server. Use a controlled private connection or HTTPS gateway for Supabase and an encrypted restricted PostgreSQL route; never expose port 5432 broadly. No cloud Supabase fallback is introduced.
+
+Do not apply historical prototype migrations to the adopted production schema. Preserve existing IDs and data. Live database schema changes still require backup, restore verification and owner approval.
+
+## Browser test codes (preview only)
+
+The app still requests and verifies OTP through Supabase Auth. No code is accepted locally and no browser action grants admin access.
+
+For an isolated DEVELOPMENT database, configure matching test-number mappings in Auth and the app. In the self-hosted Auth container use GOTRUE_SMS_TEST_OTP (digits-only international phone: six digits, comma-separated) and GOTRUE_SMS_TEST_OTP_VALID_UNTIL. Recreate only the Auth service after reviewing its effective Compose configuration. Do not enable automatic phone confirmation.
+
+App environment:
+
+- APP_ENV=preview
+- DATABASE_ENV=development
+- SUPABASE_PREVIEW_TEST_OTPS: exactly the same mapping as Auth
+- PREVIEW_OTP_VALID_UNTIL: explicit future ISO timestamp
+
+Only mapped test numbers receive a visible browser code; other numbers require the real SMS provider. Missing, expired, or production settings never expose a code. Remove the Auth mapping and app mapping before production. This tests the signup flow, not ownership of a real phone. Test accounts must use a separate development database; these settings are not active on the owner's production server.
+
+## AI configuration
+
+Provider keys are backend environment variables: GEMINI_API_KEY, AI_FORZA_API_KEY (legacy alias ai-forza supported). Worker origins: PART_RECOGNITION_WORKER_URL and ATLAS_AI_WORKER_URL. PART_RECOGNITION_WORKER_TOKEN is the recognition worker's access token. Empty recognition origin disables that worker and allows the existing direct-provider path. Worker provider keys belong in the worker's own secret environment. Do not use VITE_* for secrets; do not save keys in database settings or commit .env.
+
+## Remaining live verification
+
+Repository checks do not prove access to the owner's server. Before claiming live completion verify /api/health, anonymous /api/runtime, signup -> Auth -> user_profiles -> chosen credentials -> login, admin role isolation, and database persistence after restart. An existing password cannot be recovered from its hash. Recover the admin username by a narrowly scoped query on the correct installation; set a new password via a secure operator flow if necessary.
+
+Railway work is cancelled at the owner's request; no Railway changes are required by this document.
+
+## Design merge 2026-10-22
+
+Integrated the design delta from atlassanatpish1 commit 32de134f801fd19814e78c82b0383b6edefb4b4d against prior application snapshot d1522f00e2ac9c2fa0ead1767ed5f9480dfd6dec, preserving the auth validation and preview configuration changes. The source main branch was re-rooted, so the merge uses the actual file delta rather than assuming shared Git ancestry. The announcements SQL is included for review, not automatically applied to production.
+
+Legacy operational database reports and archived import automation are omitted from this public source snapshot. Legal registration identifiers in AboutUsPage require owner verification and are displayed as pending confirmation. Secrets and live customer rows are excluded. The live server must be backed up, deployed and checked separately before marking this release live.
